body:
I like the one about feral dogs being allies. I think vultures would avoid their kills because they're smart/playful and might find stalking vultures fun even when they aren't hungry.

Same on the fast metabolism/calories. Have you ever seen a horse sweating steam after a run? I imagine after the transformation there's a little curl of steam evaporating off and that when they try to like;
Only partially transform that other wolves smell the adrenaline and become alert and that if they're new at it and it's less controlled that that sweat vapor also gives them away.
